ch I still use today  which is believed in the me that  believes in you and caminar essentially  uses to artificially boost Simone's  confidence because he knew that Simone  looked up to him and it's such a  brilliant phrase because nobody ever  knows how to react to it whenever I've  used it in real life  I've often gotten quite shocked  reactions and non anime fans often  praised me for my out-of-the-box  thinking which in reality is simply a  basic philosophy that I stole from an  animated man with incredibly blue hair  but why is all of this optimism talked  revelant well it's because I was  watching Gurren Lagann when it was first  airing which was while I was in my final  year of high school being 2007 and yes  that does make me old thank you for  noticing but the person I was back then  is radically different to Who I am now  I was an extremely introverted  anti-social generally depressed kid with  a deep distaste for the world in general  and no confidence in myself whatsoever  and what's worse is that while I was  watching and reading a whole ton of  other series at the time because you  know that was the only enjoyment I could  find in life living vicariously through  fictional characters but most of those  stories happen to be like really deep  and depressing properties think stuff  like Evangelion Trigon or even fate/stay  night generally darker more profound  themes that come at great expense to a  character often resulting in tragedy and  yeah I was also engaged in my optimistic  series like I was reading one piece  quickly at the time and honestly that  was a bit of a lifeline of joy for me  and still is however in 2007 everything  changed for the better  being the hardcore high school we buy  was I made it my mission to watch  anything and everything I could and  April brought us Tengen Toppa Gurren  Lagann and I was hooked from the very  first episode the art was incredibly  stylized in this super schmack manner  that really stood out from the more 