hy  really got burnt into my soul and even  though I didn't have a real life figure  like coming and saying it to me I still  took on board the general idea which is  that your own self-doubt is irrelevant  just do the thing do the thing the best  you can and if you fail then so what but  if you never try you'll never succeed  and it is amazing just how the world  unlocked when I started looking at  things this way I took opportunities I  never would have considered before and I  even learnt to create my own  opportunities which is something that  has led to pretty much every major  career decision in my adult life and  once again all thanks to the words of a  2d character a 2d character that I  should say would go on to leave me in  shock after episode eight when seemingly  out of nowhere  kameena sacrificed himself and made a  grand exit from the series now to a high  school me this was incredibly shocking  because I simply wasn't used to stories  that allowed their main characters to  you know be mortal remember this was a  time before gamer Florence popularized  the nobody is safe style of storytelling  we see a lot today and lots of my  experience in anime was stuff like  Dragon Ball where death was effectively  meaningless and when it came to the daka  series well the main character would  always like die at the end if that was  going to happen  definitely not episode 8 and this event  left me really conflicted because on the  one hand I was used to tragic depressing  events as stated before but this was it  was kind of different  this wasn't just tragic it was actually  pure heroics there was something really  bittersweet about leaving comm unit  behind because I knew that he himself  was incredibly satisfied with how he had  used his life and also this method of  sacrifice would not be restricted coming  alone because towards the end of the  series several key characters all of  whom I loved went on to embrace doing  the impossible and channeling their  lives towards the constant evolution of  humanity and each and every one of them  was another iOpener of how even in its  most tragic moments life doesn't need to  be overcome with despair because there  is almost always a path forward but on  the other hand this initial sacrifice  had left me with Simone the guy I still  didn't really like because he was too  much like me but this is where things  really kicked into gear because it was  now time  for Simone to step up and prove to every  introverted self-doubting human being on  this planet that they too could do  something amazing or barring doing  something amazing something somewhat  decent something they could do something  and even that is enough and yes I know  it's just an anime but that's the effect  watching Simone Grohe had on me like he  went through a bit of a shinji phase but  a handful of episodes later that was  done  Simone took on bought everything that  Carmina had spouted at him and he made  the active choice to live the believe in  the me who believes a new lifestyle just  from a different perspective as he went  on to inspire I guess pretty much the  entire human race leading to the defeat  of the beastmen and the end of human  oppression and yes it's all fictional  but that doesn't make it any less  inspiring to see somebody that I  identify with become someone that I  could only dream of being and it's  obviously not just Simone either I spent  a lot of time talking about both he and  Carmina but the extended cast of Gurren  Lagann is one of the finest pool of  characters you will ever find in  storytelling and they all grow to this  point of insane optimism overcoming  their own personal barriers and reaching  incredible heights as a result in fact  even the established antagonists undergo  this transformation like fear a landlord  Janome and when they all come together  at the end well that's one of the most  satisfying conclusions to a story that I  have ever experienced speaking of there  you